issue_context.body:
### Description

When using the activity tracking option on Microsoft extension logging logger factory to add baggage and tags from current tracing context adding tags to the log scope works good regarding the placement of key value pairs to the scope, and can be propagated to every exporter correctly, but when trying to add baggage to the scope each item is included such that the key for the scope is null and the value for the scope is the list of baggage items enumerated , because of that some log exporters don't pick up the scope because the key is null.

![image](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/assets/59967231/59eaabb2-04cd-439f-a234-35c17d7ab5bc)

the difference is between scope 1 and 2 in the picture above


### Reproduction Steps

Used the weather forecast .net example and added instrumentation with activity tracking option a console exporter and open telemetry tracer.
this is instrumentation part of my service registration:

```c#
builder.Services
    .AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(traceBuilder =>
    {
        traceBuilder
        .SetResourceBuilder(ResourceBuilder.CreateDefault().AddService("TestOtel"))
        .AddSource(Instrumentation.ActivitySourceName)
        .SetSampler(new AlwaysOnSampler())
        .AddHttpClientInstrumentation()
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddConsoleExporter();
    });


builder.Logging
    .ClearProviders()
    .Configure(options => options.ActivityTrackingOptions = ActivityTrackingOptions.TraceId | ActivityTrackingOptions.SpanId | ActivityTrackingOptions.Baggage | ActivityTrackingOptions.Tags)
    .AddOpenTelemetry(options =>
{
    options.IncludeScopes = true;
    options.SetResourceBuilder(ResourceBuilder.CreateDefault().AddService("TestOtel"));
    options.AddConsoleExporter();
    options.AddGenevaLogExporter(exporterOptions =>
    {
        exporterOptions.ConnectionString = "EtwSession=OpenTelemetry";
        exporterOptions.ExceptionStackExportMode = ExceptionStackExportMode.ExportAsString;
        exporterOptions.EventNameExportMode = EventNameExportMode.ExportAsPartAName;
    });
});
``` 

this is my controller:
```c#
        [HttpGet(Name = "GetWeatherForecast")]
        public IEnumerable<WeatherForecast> Get()
        {
            using var activityTest = _instrumentation.ActivitySource.StartActivity("TestActivity");
            activityTest?.SetBaggage("BagKeyFirst", "BagValueFirst");
            activityTest?.SetBaggage("BagKeySecond", "BagValueSecond");
            activityTest?.SetTag("TagKeyFirst", "tagValueFirst");
            activityTest?.SetTag("TagKeySecond", "tagValueSecond");
            var placeholder = "actual runntime value";
            _logger.LogInformation("{testPlaceHolder}", placeholder);

            return Enumerable.Range(1, 5).Select(index => new WeatherForecast
            {
                Date = DateTime.Now.AddDays(index),
                TemperatureC = Random.Shared.Next(-20, 55),
                Summary = Summaries[Random.Shared.Next(Summaries.Length)]
            })
            .ToArray();
        }
``` 


### Expected behavior

the baggage will be added to the scope with a key so that exporters ( specifically the geneva log exporter) will be able to pick it up and send forward

### Actual behavior

the baggage is added to the scope without a key or with null key and so ignored by some exporters

### Regression?

_No response_

### Known Workarounds

_No response_

### Configuration

.net 6 

### Other information

_No response_

