@yoziv what kind of logger and `IExternalScopeProvider` is used to produce the output you are showing? The baggage scope is produced as [`IEnumerable<KeyValuePair<string, string>>`](https://source.dot.net/#Microsoft.Extensions.Logging/LoggerFactoryScopeProvider.cs,223) and implement `ToString()` which produce the output you are seeing in the output. The used logger `IExternalScopeProvider.ForEachScope` is the callback which gets the scope object and handles it. 
The Tags scope is exposed as `IEnumerable<KeyValuePair<string, object>>` which looks the handled differently than the baggage in your case with the used logger/exporter.  

CC @CodeBlanch @cijothomas

@tarekgh, should the Json console formatter also support `IEnumerable<KeyValuePair<string, string>>` ?

https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/38166fba8921a572e82c6ac3342ef0e2afa7b73e/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Console/src/JsonConsoleFormatter.cs#L106-L122

```json
{
    "EventId": 0,
    "LogLevel": "Information",
    "Category": "HomeController",
    "Message": "Hello World!",
    "State": {
        "Message": "Hello World!",
        "{OriginalFormat}": "Hello World!"
    },
    "Scopes": [
        {
            "Message": "TagKeyFirst:tagValueFirst, TagKeySecond:tagValueSecond",
            "TagKeyFirst": "tagValueFirst",
            "TagKeySecond": "tagValueSecond"
        },
        "BagKeySecond:BagValueSecond, BagKeyFirst:BagValueFirst" <= not the same format as tags
    ]
}
```
